From 9d90fa134679bbf122ee582aba5f7573d33addb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] MSL: Fragment outputs take their color attachment's numeric
 type

STEAMAC-2C: a Left 4 Dead 2 pipeline (DXVK) writes an unsigned integer
output to an R32_SINT color attachment. Vulkan only leaves the values written
undefined when the output's numeric type differs from the attachment's
(KosmicKrisp writes the output's bits), but Metal fails the render pipeline:
"output of type uint4 is not compatible with a MTLPixelFormatR32Sint color
attachment", and Venus skipped every draw with that pipeline.

Add Options::frag_output_float_mask, frag_output_sint_mask and
frag_output_uint_mask: bit N marks the color attachment at location N as
floating-point/normalized, signed or unsigned integer. A fragment output of
another numeric type is declared in the output struct with the attachment's
(same width; 8-bit integers to a float attachment become half), the shader
writes a local of its own type, and the local is bit cast to the member on
return (converted where the widths differ), with padding as before. This
covers plain outputs, output arrays (per element location) and outputs packed
into the components of one location. Locations in none of the masks keep
their type.
